  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adaptation in Ecologically Critical Areas of Bangladesh (AECAB)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is targeting communities in the Sundarbans and Hakaluki Haor regions and is committed to ensuring that at least 40% of the project beneficiaries will represent women, people with disability (PWD), indigenous people, and religious and ethnic minorities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will increasing the resilience of vulnerable communities whilst delivering ecosystem-based protection and restoration of the Sundarbans and Hakaluki Haor. The approach comprises of six interlinked pillars, i.e. climate and weather information services, climate resilient WASH services, climate resilient Infrastructure and technical knowhow, renewable energy solutions, climate resilient and nature positive livelihood practices and locally led adaptation approach (LLA) for Nature Based Services (NBS).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is one of the major steps towards meeting the Bangladesh Government&apos;s commitments to biodiversity conservation, climate action, Sustainable Development Goals, the Sendai Framework and the Paris Agreement. This will be acheived through:Outcome 1: Locally-led initiatives to protect and restore Ecologically Critical Areas (ECAs) in  the Sundarbans and Hakaluki Haor Outcome 2: Improved climate resilient and nature positive livelihood practices and energy solutions Outcome 3: Improved protection and increased accessibility to climate resilient homes, infrastructure and WASH facilities Outcome 4: Improved productivity and reduced loss &amp; damage and sufferings from climate shocks and stresses</narrative>
  </description>
